{"title":"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Basically_1_but_less_complicated)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Basically 1 but less complicated)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with a radius of 1 and a circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with a radius of 4 are externally tangent. A third circle is tangent to the first two and to one of their common external tangents as shown. What is the radius of the third circle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e0340e3581aab9d635bcf2dca6b71152f8fa5290.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.75cm); pair A=(0,1), B=(4,4); dot(A); dot(B); draw( circle(A,1) ); draw( circle(B,4) ); draw( (-1.5,0)--(8.5,0) ); draw( A -- (A+(-1,0)) ); label(&quot;$1$&quot;, A -- (A+(-1,0)), N ); draw( B -- (B+(4,0)) ); label(&quot;$4$&quot;, B -- (B+(4,0)), N ); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,E); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,W);  filldraw( circle( (12/9,4/9), 4/9 ), lightgray, black ); dot( (12/9,4/9) ); [/asy]\" width=\"358\" height=\"285\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c46571f8fa181c3b9db93905a50be3f399f2f38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }\\frac {1}{3} \\qquad \\text{(B) }\\frac {2}{5} \\qquad \\text{(C) }\\frac {5}{12} \\qquad \\text{(D) }\\frac {4}{9} \\qquad \\text{(E) }\\frac {1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"358\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77ff0006500e55413b38636a2c80caba13c7591d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1cm); pair A=(0,1), B=(4,4), C=(4,1), S=(12/9,4/9); dot(A); dot(B); draw( circle(A,1) ); draw( circle(B,4) ); draw( (-1.5,0)--(8.5,0) ); draw( (A+(4,0)) -- A -- (A+(0,-1)) ); draw( A -- B -- (B+(0,-4)) ); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,E); label(&quot;$S$&quot;,S,N);  filldraw( circle(S,4/9), lightgray, black ); dot(S); draw( rightanglemark(A,C,B) ); draw( S -- A ); draw( S -- B ); [/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"382\" />\n</p><p>In the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c242a7728e5f1db53dd3e72975555dc7de063e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 1+4 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/93391cdcf89bb0c73ea030e8dafd82e2b587d30a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4-1 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"126\" height=\"13\" />, thus by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/5/025c2061366089f53fc13fb726784f6e27c592c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of the small circle, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the perpendicular distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. Moreover, the small circle is tangent to both other circles, hence we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db007c88064f8413a603bd1644930798949a5cdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SA=1+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/587677b99667f2ac05d54a7f8d9382bacf0dbe20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SB=4+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/4/b94d8449b7fd564941094995d76ba7bf4642bb0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SA = \\sqrt{s^2 + (1-r)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"168\" height=\"32\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/8/5c8d839d37a6e733e7c363ddb15ea531679666c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SB=\\sqrt{(4-s)^2 + (4-r)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"214\" height=\"32\" />. Hence we get the following two equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b633bdaf544dac41dcf32fa08d266db16af77fc0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} s^2 + (1-r)^2 &amp; = (1+r)^2 \\\\ (4-s)^2 + (4-r)^2 &amp; = (4+r)^2 \\end{align*}\" width=\"228\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying both, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3fcad2ce3c9aa7fc826d7dcaa20bd9861da0bab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} s^2 &amp; = 4r \\\\ (4-s)^2 &amp; = 16r \\end{align*}\" width=\"110\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>As in our case both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive, we can divide the second one by the first one to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/4789e7958da801d1d2f7c24b33939cbf098ea346.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\frac{4-s}s \\right)^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"110\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>Now there are two possibilities: either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/a/f4aab9bdfe86c118cb2cb25649bc2ce4910c93fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4-s}s=-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f00627ff596b1c9b3dafada24a0be0da0979287c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4-s}s=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"76\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>In the first case clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06ad541cbecf5f5f7aaea6ff0ba6da582c34da30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, which puts the center on the wrong side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, so this is not the correct case. \n</p><p>(Note: This case corresponds to the other circle that is tangent to both given circles and the common tangent line. By coincidence, due to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff3c81ca2426fed69bc7607dde1f79286c1b855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" /> ratio between radii of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, this circle turns out to have the same radius as circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, with center directly left of center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> directly above center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.) \n</p><p>The second case solves to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9aedbfc62dca2dd39ffcd87d31f0e5fb5200ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=\\frac 43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" />. We then have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b22f2e24e9146045b98b908c34c77192d4b85a8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4r = s^2 = \\frac {16}9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/532b82697841d67905f403a40bc399673ac66ade.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\boxed{\\frac 49}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"57\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nMore generally, for two large circles of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, the radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> of the small circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/8991bcf99334f033a24c8addd4b773dedc886830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{ab}{\\left(\\sqrt{a}+\\sqrt{b}\\right)^2} = \\frac{1}{\\left(1/\\sqrt{a}+1/\\sqrt{b}\\right)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -34px\" width=\"300\" height=\"60\" />. \n</p><p>Equivalently, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/2/3d2b8f17f26542b479da528216cf4b2f2ac346f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/\\sqrt{c} = 1/\\sqrt{a} + 1/\\sqrt{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The horizontal line is the equivalent of a circle of curvature <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, thus we can apply <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Descartes%27_Circle_Formula\" title=\"Descartes&#39; Circle Formula\">Descartes' Circle Formula</a>.\n</p><p>The four circles have curvatures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/c/d8ceb79dccef41a843dee3d3323352cbdb3a405e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 1, \\frac 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6e37acedc7ba935b5670cc3a9eea6188f9127d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 1r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fdcc9a0a1a1a2cffdc6daf2bd0d04bf2e97eb75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\left(0^2+1^2+\\frac {1}{4^2}+\\frac{1}{r^2}\\right)=\\left(0+1+\\frac 14+\\frac 1r\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"346\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecb05776cd2b4ae5c0e10f32694df5a1cd4054e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{34}{16}+\\frac{2}{r^2}=\\frac{25}{16}+\\frac{5}{2r}+\\frac{1}{r^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"195\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c957bc84cc47e83e5e9884502b84a138490bfc1b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{r^2}-\\frac{5}{2r}+\\frac{9}{16}=0\\]\" width=\"139\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/d/e4d794221ddb24371d77ede48efe233cb2f2eeb6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{16}{r^2}-\\frac{40}{r}+9=0\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65bf17396c32cd68738bb5351df8bb5947ff5633.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{4}{r}-9\\right)\\left(\\frac{4}{r}-1\\right)=0\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cannot equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/532b82697841d67905f403a40bc399673ac66ade.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\boxed{\\frac 49}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"57\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Basically_1_but_less_complicated.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Basically_1_but_less_complicated)\">Solution 3 (Basically 1 but less complicated)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Basically 1 but less complicated)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>As in solution 1, in triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c242a7728e5f1db53dd3e72975555dc7de063e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 1+4 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/93391cdcf89bb0c73ea030e8dafd82e2b587d30a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4-1 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"126\" height=\"13\" />, thus by the Pythagorean theorem or pythagorean triples in general, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/5/025c2061366089f53fc13fb726784f6e27c592c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the perpendicular intersecting point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/8/778af50b2583d0f131791bad32ff52c47db53189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547263eb631ff2f1ef193c447d92ecb966213e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" /> both perpendicular radii, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> form a rectangle. We just have to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> now. From the Pythagorean theorem and subtracting to get lengths, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/1/b815a8d2f6b286546cb6de0c5bbe497db62577e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=s=4=\\sqrt{(r+1)^2 - (1-r)^2} + \\sqrt{(r+4)^2 - (4-r)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"469\" height=\"35\" />, which is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8dd600094cef17df244a7af2c8d99de0eb9a9372.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4=\\sqrt{4r}+\\sqrt{16r} \\implies \\sqrt{r}=\\frac{2}{3} \\implies r= \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{4}{9}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"391\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~Wezzerwez7254\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zOwYoFOUg2U\">https://youtu.be/zOwYoFOUg2U</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12\" title=\"2001 AMC 12\">2001 AMC 12</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_